---
import InteriorLayout from "../layouts/InteriorLayout.astro";
import Container from "../components/Container.astro";

// Every disclosure below is based on what the site actually does, not a
// template: Netlify (hosting + Netlify Forms, which records IP/user
// agent/referrer with each submission), Zapier -> Jobber (form
// submissions forwarded to the CRM - client-confirmed, configured outside
// this repo), Mux (video hosting + Mux Data playback analytics, which is
// on by default and sets the `muxData` cookie), and Meta - the Pixel in
// LandingLayout plus the Conversions API in
// netlify/functions/submission-created.mjs, both limited to the
// /free-estimate pages and quiz. No other analytics or trackers exist in
// the codebase. If any of that changes, this page needs to change with
// it - and bump the date.
// Contact is phone-only because that's the only verified method; swap in
// a dedicated privacy email once the client has one.
const EFFECTIVE_DATE = "October 1, 2026";
---

<InteriorLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Triple R Roofing"
  description="How Triple R Roofing collects, uses, and shares information submitted through this website."
  headerAlwaysSolid
>
  <article class="policy">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <header class="policy__header">
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
        <h1 class="policy__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="policy__date">Effective Date: {EFFECTIVE_DATE}</p>
      </header>

      <div class="policy__body">
        <p>
          This policy explains what information Triple R Roofing collects
          through this website, how we use it, and who helps us handle it.
          We&rsquo;re a roofing company serving Sacramento, California and
          the surrounding areas.
        </p>

        <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Information you give us.</strong> When you request a free
          estimate through our contact form, we collect:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>your name</li>
          <li>your phone number</li>
          <li>your email address, if you choose to provide it</li>
          <li>the address of the property you need help with</li>
          <li>the service you need</li>
          <li>any message you include</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          On our free estimate landing page, our short questionnaire collects
          your first and last name, phone number, email address, city, the
          services you&rsquo;re interested in, how you plan to pay (financing,
          cash, insurance, or not sure yet), and any project details you add.
        </p>
        <p>You don&rsquo;t have to use either form; you can always call us instead.</p>
        <p>
          <strong>Information collected with your request.</strong> When you
          submit a form, our form provider also records your IP address,
          browser type, and the page you submitted it from. If you reached our
          landing page by clicking one of our ads, we also record which ad
          campaign the link came from.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Information collected automatically.</strong> Like most
          websites, our hosting provider automatically receives basic
          technical information when you visit. That includes your IP
          address, browser and device type, and the pages you request. This
          is needed to deliver the site and keep it secure.
        </p>
        <p>
          Some pages include videos hosted by Mux. When a video loads or
          plays, Mux collects information about playback: whether it loaded
          and played smoothly, plus your device, browser, approximate
          location based on your IP address, and a random viewer ID. This
          helps measure and improve video performance. It&rsquo;s described
          in more detail under Cookies below.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our free estimate landing pages use the Meta Pixel, an advertising
          tool from Meta (the company behind Facebook and Instagram). It&rsquo;s
          described under How We Share Information. The rest of our website
          doesn&rsquo;t use advertising pixels or third-party analytics like
          Google Analytics.
        </p>

        <h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <p>We use the information you submit to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>respond to your estimate or service request</li>
          <li>contact you about your request by phone, text message, or email</li>
          <li>schedule inspections, estimates, or roofing work</li>
          <li>provide customer service</li>
          <li>keep appropriate business records</li>
          <li>operate and improve our website and services</li>
          <li>
            measure how well our advertising works, including which ads lead
            to estimate requests
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How We Share Information</h2>
        <p>
          We don&rsquo;t sell your personal information for money. We share
          it with service providers that help us run the website and our
          business, and we use Meta&rsquo;s advertising tools as described
          below:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Netlify</strong> hosts this website. It also receives,
            stores, and filters spam from contact form submissions.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Zapier</strong> automatically passes contact form
            submissions from our website to our customer management system.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Jobber</strong> is the customer management system we use
            to keep track of customer requests, contact details, and
            scheduling for estimates and roofing work.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Mux</strong> hosts and streams the videos on this website
            and collects video playback information as described above.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Meta</strong> provides the advertising tools we use for our
            ads on Facebook and Instagram. When you visit our free estimate
            landing pages, the Meta Pixel sends Meta information about your
            visit, such as the pages you view, your progress through the
            questionnaire, and your IP address and browser information. If you
            submit the questionnaire, we also send Meta a record of your
            request. That record includes your email address, phone number,
            name, and city in hashed (coded) form, plus your IP address,
            browser information, the services you selected, and how you plan
            to pay. Meta uses this to match your request to our ads and
            measure their results. Meta may also use information it receives
            under its own terms and privacy policy, including to improve its
            advertising services.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We may also disclose information if required by law, or to protect
          our rights, our customers, or others.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          The main pages of our website don&rsquo;t use advertising cookies.
          Two services set cookies:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Mux</strong> sets a cookie called <code>muxData</code> when
            a video loads. It holds a random viewer ID and session information
            so Mux can measure video performance, and it expires after one
            year.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Meta</strong> sets its own cookies (such as
            <code>_fbp</code> and <code>_fbc</code>) on our free estimate
            landing pages to recognize your browser and connect your visit to
            our ads.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          When you submit the questionnaire, we also save a temporary ID in
          your browser&rsquo;s session storage so the same request isn&rsquo;t
          counted twice. It&rsquo;s cleared when you close the tab.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings, and you
          can manage how Meta uses your information for ads in your Facebook
          or Instagram ad settings.
        </p>

        <h2>Third-Party Services and Links</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Netlify</strong> (website hosting and form handling): see
            Netlify&rsquo;s privacy policy.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Zapier</strong> (form automation): see Zapier&rsquo;s
            privacy policy.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Jobber</strong> (customer management): see Jobber&rsquo;s
            privacy policy.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Mux</strong> (video hosting): see Mux&rsquo;s privacy
            policy for how it handles playback data.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Meta</strong> (advertising): see Meta&rsquo;s privacy
            policy.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Wisetack</strong> (financing): our website doesn&rsquo;t
            collect financing applications or send any information to
            Wisetack. If you apply for financing through Wisetack, your
            application goes to Wisetack and is covered by Wisetack&rsquo;s
            own privacy policy and terms.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Google reviews</strong>: our link to our Google reviews
            takes you to Google&rsquo;s website, which is covered by
            Google&rsquo;s privacy policy.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>We&rsquo;re not responsible for the privacy practices of websites we link to.</p>

        <h2>Do Not Track</h2>
        <p>
          Some browsers can send a &ldquo;Do Not Track&rdquo; signal.
          There&rsquo;s no common standard for responding to these signals,
          and this website doesn&rsquo;t currently change its behavior when
          it receives one.
        </p>
        <p>
          On our free estimate landing pages, Meta may collect information
          about your online activity over time and across different websites
          through the Meta Pixel and its cookies. The rest of our website
          doesn&rsquo;t allow third parties to collect information for that
          purpose.
        </p>

        <h2>Data Security</h2>
        <p>
          We use reasonable measures to protect the information you send us,
          including encrypted (HTTPS) connections to this website. No method
          of sending or storing information over the internet is completely
          secure, so we can&rsquo;t guarantee absolute security.
        </p>

        <h2>Data Retention</h2>
        <p>
          We keep the information you submit only as long as reasonably
          needed for the purposes described in this policy. That includes
          responding to your request, providing services, and keeping records
          as our business and legal obligations require.
        </p>

        <h2>Your Choices</h2>
        <p>
          You can call us to ask to see, correct, or delete the information
          you submitted through our website. We&rsquo;ll respond as required
          by applicable law. We may need to verify your identity, and we may
          keep certain information when we&rsquo;re legally required or
          permitted to.
        </p>

        <h2>Children&rsquo;s Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          This website is for people looking for roofing and home services.
          It isn&rsquo;t directed to children under 13, and we don&rsquo;t
          knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If
          you believe a child has sent us information, call us and we&rsquo;ll
          delete it.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy from time to time. When we do, we&rsquo;ll
          post the updated version here and change the effective date at the
          top.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact Us</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions about this policy or your information, contact
          Triple R Roofing:
        </p>
        <p class="policy__contact">
          <strong>Phone:</strong> <a href="tel:+19164205635">(916) 420-5635</a><br />
          <strong>Hours:</strong> Mon&ndash;Sun, 6 AM&ndash;7 PM
        </p>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </article>
</InteriorLayout>

<style>
  /* A plain reading page - no cards, rules, or icons. Hierarchy comes
     from type alone, on the site's own cream background. */
  .policy {
    background: var(--color-bg);
    padding-top: calc(var(--nav-height) + var(--space-9));
    padding-bottom: var(--space-9);
  }

  @media (max-width: 899px) {
    .policy {
      padding-top: calc(var(--nav-height) + var(--space-7));
      padding-bottom: var(--space-8);
    }
  }

  .policy__header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .policy__title {
    font-size: var(--text-h2);
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .policy__date {
    font-size: var(--text-body-sm);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .policy__body {
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .policy__body h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-h5);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    font-stretch: var(--stretch-normal);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .policy__body p,
  .policy__body li {
    line-height: var(--leading-normal);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .policy__body p {
    max-width: none;
  }

  .policy__body ul {
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  .policy__body li::marker {
    color: var(--color-accent-strong);
  }

  .policy__body code {
    font-family: inherit;
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .policy__body a {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
  }

  .policy__contact {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }
</style>
